# 1Password references ONLY. Never a resolved value.
#
# These point at the "Agent" vault: the pool of credentials you are willing
# to share with agents. bootstrap.sh resolves them into per-agent tmpfs
# directories that containers mount read-only. Nothing here ever enters an
# image or a container's environment block.
#
#   ./scripts/bootstrap.sh          # picks up ~/.op-token on its own
#   op run --env-file=.env -- ./scripts/bootstrap.sh    # or drive it yourself
#
# Create each item in 1Password as an "API Credential", which gives you a
# field named `credential`. Change the paths below if you name them
# differently -- nothing in the code depends on these particular titles.

# --- agent identity: claude-code -------------------------------------------
# From `claude setup-token` on a machine with a terminal. Interactive: a
# human has to run it. See README, "What remains manual".
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN="op://Agent/Claude Code OAuth Token/credential"

# Alternative to the line above, and the one to prefer if you would rather
# not put a subscription token on an always-on box: an API key bills per
# token and needs nobody at a keyboard. Either one satisfies the container.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="op://Agent/Anthropic API Key/credential"

# Optional: a GitHub token scoped to the repos agents may push. Also what
# lets bootstrap clone over HTTPS, since this box has no SSH key.
GH_TOKEN="op://Agent/GitHub Agent Token/credential"

# --- agent identity: hermes -------------------------------------------------
# Local OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Usually needs no key; set one only if
# your server enforces it.
# HERMES_API_KEY="op://Agent/Hermes API Key/credential"

# --- agent identity: agentcore ----------------------------------------------
# An IAM user whose only permission is invoking the two AgentCore harnesses
# named in config/agents.toml. Its own identity, so the coding agents never
# see these and it never sees theirs.
# Field names vary by how the item was created: an API Credential item has
# `username` and `credential`, while a custom one usually has whatever you
# typed. If a reference does not resolve, bootstrap prints the item's
# actual field labels -- copy one in rather than guessing.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="op://Agent/PharmacyChecker AWS Agent Orchestrator IAM User/access key id"
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="op://Agent/PharmacyChecker AWS Agent Orchestrator IAM User/secret access key"

# --- identity: voice (phase two) --------------------------------------------
# The realtime voice bridge. Its own identity, so the coding agents never
# see these and it never sees theirs.
OPENAI_API_KEY="op://Agent/OpenAI API Key/credential"
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN="op://Agent/Discord Bot Token/credential"
# Signs the incoming-call webhook, so only OpenAI can make the phone ring.
# From the webhook settings in the OpenAI dashboard.
OPENAI_WEBHOOK_SECRET="op://Agent/OpenAI Webhook Secret/credential"
